{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/73720-scars","id":73720,"title":"Scars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-17T08:04:51-08:00","id":73720,"title":"Scars?","content":"Just had a quick question, in B&amp;S it says aggravated damage causes scars on kindred, but it also says that a vampire who wants to keep scars as mementos or for others reasons has to spend willpower to keep them. So if you were burnt would the scars go away or stay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2306-gnomeflinger007","name":"gnomeflinger007","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2306_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T08:21:56-08:00","id":73726,"title":"","content":"Aggravated damage leaves scars. However, if you want to keep a scar gained from lethal/bashing damage, you can pay willpower to keep it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T08:25:13-08:00","id":73730,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to remove a scar from aggravated? example if a kindred was burned would cutting away the flesh and letting it regrow eliminate the scars? or other means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2306-gnomeflinger007","name":"gnomeflinger007","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2306_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T08:29:52-08:00","id":73732,"title":"","content":"Well... As far as book says - No. Just as having your hand burned, does not allow you to cut it further away and regrow it as lethal... <br /> However, if you want to hide them, you can easily ask your local Sanctified Priest or an Acolyte to weave a simple ritual to remove it. Of course, it's temporary, but it could easily have a duration of 3-6 months, meaning that it shouldn't be too costly or inconvenient to repeat the constant ritual.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T11:56:17-08:00","id":73818,"title":"","content":"You can remove the scarring from aggravated damage if you prefer without changing the game significantly. You could house rule willpower can also be used to remove scars. In the latter case, you should probably require damaging and healing the affected area or a ritual in addition to the willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T11:58:48-08:00","id":73822,"title":"","content":"While Kindred sleep, they return to the time of their Embrace. Anything that wouldn\u2019t constitute a Health level of damage heals automatically and returns to its original state pg.91 in B&amp;S. Confuses me what is a health level of damage? why wouldn't the scars revert after the aggravated is healed? Also i love the fast replies nice active forums<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2306-gnomeflinger007","name":"gnomeflinger007","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2306_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T14:06:49-08:00","id":73874,"title":"","content":"A box marked with damge on the Health track. Not all changes to the vampire body imply marking those boxes. For example, a piercing, or a haircut, or even the effects of damage negated by Resilience (wich still leave wound marks like bullet holes or rent flesh, even if you mark no Health box).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T14:18:32-08:00","id":73878,"title":"","content":"oh gotcha, still kinda new to WoD. My GM fried my pretty little vamp and Im just trying to see what my options are, rp crispy critter or find some way to remove the damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2306-gnomeflinger007","name":"gnomeflinger007","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2306_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T15:08:27-08:00","id":73902,"title":"","content":"I note with some interest that aggravated damage leaving scars adds to the mitigating factors of the Tainted Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T15:55:56-08:00","id":73927,"title":"","content":"Typically, vampires that suffer aggravated damage to eventually heal to the point where they look like they healed the damage naturally. Vampires don't have the power to undo the changes to appearance from such extensive damage.<br /> <br /> As someone mentioned earlier, vampires automatically &quot;heal&quot; things like hair loss, tattoos, piercings, clipped finger nails, and other cosmetic changes. For some vampires, this is quite annoying. Imagine having to shave a long beard or cut long hair every night. There was a vampire story in one of the books where a vampire was embraced with a half clipped finger nail and had to fix it every night (he eventually did it like clockwork with laser guided precision using his teeth a decade after his embrace). Its for reasons like that, that vampires often offer their childer a chance to groom themselves properly before the embrace as they will remain that way forever. How a vampire was embraced will determine what they have to work with and the level of upkeep they will have (many vampires make a habit of keeping tools like wigs or professional makeup artists).<br /> <br /> The whole part of spending a point of willpower to make permanent changes is not a well known fact among vampires (except the dragons as it is their entire point of being is to change their bodies and natures, and its good proof that changes can happen). If most vampires don't know that, then maybe there are tricks most vampires don't know of that allow them to make further change their undying bodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T18:38:30-08:00","id":74013,"title":"","content":"I forgot about this one. A vampire could in theory get surgery done to fix scars and other signs damage, but they would need to spend willpower to make changes hold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T05:59:27-07:00","id":529823,"title":"","content":"Sorry to resurrect this thread... I have a question about ghouls and healing scars. I thought it would be fitting to throw it in here. If you make someone a ghoul who already has some nasty scars, could said ghoul spend vitae to heal up the past damage? Perhaps like a vampire healing aggravated 5 vitae to do that? or perhaps a will power spent? What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T06:54:45-07:00","id":529889,"title":"","content":"As a vampire cannot heal his past scarred, I'd say that a ghoul can't heal them either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T06:58:26-07:00","id":529892,"title":"","content":"Vampires are stuck at the time of embrace. A ghoul is still mostly human with the ability to heal. if a vampire can heal a scar without breaking the game, do you think it would be acceptable for a ghoul to heal a scar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T07:06:35-07:00","id":529900,"title":"","content":"Scars on humans typically don't go away, depending on the kind of scar. I've got a scar on my left arm from when I gouged myself on a broken soda can tab from well over a decade ago, for instance (I think it's a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypertrophic_scar\" target=\"_blank\">hypertrophic scar</a>). I don't think that a vampire or a ghoul can <i>fix</i> scarification except in the way that normal humans do, which is to say medical treatment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T07:15:21-07:00","id":529929,"title":"","content":"I can see your point. I have a scar across my stomach too, nasty thing 12 years ago, it's not going anywhere, but we arent supernatural creatures with vitae that carries the power to heal. A ghoul and a vampire can get their arms lopped off and spend vitae to reattach them, we cant. A ghoul can get shot and spend vitae to seal up the wound, we cant. I get the vampire cant heal scars they got before the embrace, because it specifically says that they are stuck that way. Even with that line of thought Are you both still thinking that ghouls cant heal a scar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T07:29:10-07:00","id":529931,"title":"","content":"A scar is a fully healed wound. You can't &quot;heal&quot; a scar, because it isn't injured, it's just the way your skin looks when heathy now. A ghoul could probably get a tattoo to cover it up, or cosmetic surgery to hide it, but no amount of Vitae is going to heal a scar, any more than it could &quot;heal&quot; a birth mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T07:31:40-07:00","id":529932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/73720-scars?p=73902#post73902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I note with some interest that aggravated damage leaving scars adds to the mitigating factors of the Tainted Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just thinking about this recently. I <i>love</i> the idea of diablerists with burn scars hidden under sleeves or socks. Kind of like the vampire version of track marks.<br /> <br /> As far as the greater topic goes, as written I suppose vampires keep their aggravated damage scars much the same way humans do. They might get smaller or fainter over time, depending on how severe they are, but never really go away.<br /> <br /> There are a couple ways you could handle it, and I think cutting off the scarred area and regrowing it completely would yield fresh, un-scarred flesh I don't see the scars as completely &quot;resetting&quot; the vampire's form in an overall sense. So cutting off a scarred hand and regrowing it will result in a hand that looks the same as it did at the moment of Embrace.<br /> <br /> Alternatively there are a couple Covenant tricks that could handle it. Blood magic, certainly. Night Doctor Surgery, and Flesh Graft Treatment also come to mind.<br /> <br /> As for ghouls: I need to read it again, but I think using vitae to heal is not like natural healing. I'd run it the same as vampire healing. Aggravated damage leaves scars that they can't &quot;heal&quot; further, but lethal damage just regenerates as if it never was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T08:41:15-07:00","id":529997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/73720-scars?p=529932#post529932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for ghouls: I need to read it again, but I think using vitae to heal is not like natural healing. I'd run it the same as vampire healing. Aggravated damage leaves scars that they can't &quot;heal&quot; further, but lethal damage just regenerates as if it never was.</div> </div> </div> </div>But unlike vampires, ghouls don't have a moment of embrace to &quot;reset&quot; to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T08:47:37-07:00","id":530001,"title":"","content":"Sure, I get that. I just don't care for running supernatural, stolen-life-fueled healing as just super-fast natural healing. Feels weird. <br /> <br /> If it's written that way somewhere, then, fine, but I don't recall seeing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T08:53:14-07:00","id":530006,"title":"","content":"Nah, I don't think it's specifically called out anywhere as working that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T08:54:23-07:00","id":530008,"title":"","content":"Maybe if we go back to <i>Ghouls</i>. Been a while since I poked around in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:00:54-07:00","id":530012,"title":"","content":"Ghouls have the moment their aging was stopped by the vampire who fed them vitae and willed them to stop aging.<br /> <br /> I'm in the camp of, It's up to the player to decide what their character looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:19:02-07:00","id":530038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/73720-scars?p=529931#post529931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A scar is a fully healed wound. You can't &quot;heal&quot; a scar, because it isn't injured, it's just the way your skin looks when heathy now. A ghoul could probably get a tattoo to cover it up, or cosmetic surgery to hide it, but no amount of Vitae is going to heal a scar, any more than it could &quot;heal&quot; a birth mark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point there that it is a fully healed wound, but it is still damaged skin. You might be healthy and it might be fine, but ultimately it is still damaged (injured) because humans dont have the ability to regenerate or heal like a ghoul. A birthmark is not damaged, it is in your genes, something entirely different.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T12:49:12-07:00","id":532131,"title":"","content":"Does lethal and bashing damage that rolls over into aggravated, leave permanent scars? Like if a vampire gets repeatedly punched, all the way into torpor and <i>nearly</i> into final death, would that leave them scarred the same way fire or sunlight would?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T13:11:41-07:00","id":532156,"title":"","content":"Doll Face Merit from Mekhet clanbook could help to heal aggravated wounds without scars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T13:06:52-07:00","id":533570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/73720-scars?p=532131#post532131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does lethal and bashing damage that rolls over into aggravated, leave permanent scars? Like if a vampire gets repeatedly punched, all the way into torpor and <i>nearly</i> into final death, would that leave them scarred the same way fire or sunlight would?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would leave a different kind of scar, as would aggravated damage claw wounds. But yeah, I think getting bone pulverized, flesh pulped and muscle shredded to the point of being aggravated damage would leave some nasty-looking crap behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}